WEBVTT

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.360
Hm? What's the matter?

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.010
Where do you think we bought these?

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.640
Where do you think we bought these?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:26.750
Wow! Look at you! You look so cute!

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:31.000
That outfit is sooo cute!
You look really good in it!

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.500
So you know, it was actually super cheap!

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.760
No way! Really? Where'd you buy it?

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.550
It starts with an "S" and ends with an "A".

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.770
I can't figure it out!

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:49.270
Well, it's a secret!

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.610
I see...

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.270
A secret, huh?

00:02:55.780 --> 00:03:00.280
When she starts high school...

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:04.740
...she'll make more friends, start texting them,

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.160
and there'll be more secrets she doesn't tell me.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.210
Hey, he's crying.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.840
What's wrong, Natsu?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.920
Nothing.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:20.340
More importantly, Hibiki, you never visit us,

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.550
then suddenly you're taking Machi shopping.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.970
Is something going... on?

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:25.850
Is something going... on?

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.770
None of your business.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.060
Looks like I struck a nerve.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.310
Oh, that's right. Yoshio came by earlier.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.690
Machi, you've work to do.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.610
I know you like that outfit, but go change.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.650
What?

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.860
Well then, I'll get going.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.950
Good luck with your work.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.750
I'll go change.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:57.710
Hibiki! Hang out with Machi again sometime!

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:02.090
What? Why would I want to hang with a kid?

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.550
You just did, today.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:07.890
I'm don't wanna play hacky sack and marbles.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:11.180
She doesn't. Just sometimes.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.560
If she wants to play,
then she should come to me.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.360
I'll teach her how adults have fun.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.400
No drugs or street racing, okay?

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.860
That's all you think I am?

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.090
Machi, did you have fun?

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.280
Yes.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.350
If you did, you should have told her.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.810
Really?

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.690
Honestly, I can't believe you turned out like this.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.360
To think that you stole a bike!

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:06.860
Dad! I'm sorry! I said, I'm sorry!

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.280
Let go of me!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.740
Shut up!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.330
You need to learn a lesson.
I'm taking you to Master Kumai.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.520
M-Machi...

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.610
He won't eat me, right?

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.070
The bear won't eat me, right?!

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:42.540
Doesn't he look kinda different
from the other day?

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.630
This is the real Natsu.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.420
Hey, what'll happen to me?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.340
You sleep here tonight.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:51.970
Huh?!

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.270
No! Anything but that!

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:57.980
Stay here and reflect on your actions.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.480
I've already reflected on them! I have!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:06.030
Hey, why is he eating a bucket?

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:08.860
Natsu likes to break wood.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.370
Oh no... That sounds like the bears at Ueno Zoo.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.790
What is that?!

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.120
Akita Prefecture's iburigakko pickles.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.540
Perhaps he's hungry.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.090
He's hungry? That's not good!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.090
Hey, that...

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.760
I think my dad drinks those.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.350
That can... is made of steel.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:43.600
Natsu's fangs can pierce steel cans.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.820
He handles the pull-tab pretty well.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:52.820
Hey, look at how much he's eating...
How hungry does he get?

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:57.410
Natsu is a gluttonous magical beast who will eat just about anything today.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:08:01.460
What? That means... I'm in serious danger!

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.210
H-He'll eat me!

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.340
Don't worry. See the box behind him?

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:11.840
That box contains offerings that villagers brought for Natsu.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:16.260
He'll distract himself by playing with items from that box.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:22.640
So be quiet, okay? Otherwise, he'll play with <i>you</i>.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:33.240
What's that?!

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.530
I can't take this anymore!

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:40.700
Glasses. For seeing well. Those are next-gen.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.410
Bears don't have good eyesight, so...

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.500
Th-That's a lie!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.750
That's a device to relieve tired eyes!

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.840
Calm down, Shota.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:50.920
He's relieving his eyes with steam so he can size me up!

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.510
He wants to see which parts of me taste good!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:08:59.510
A rice cook—

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.850
That's an oil-free fryer!

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.020
Please! Let me out!

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:07.480
He's gonna fry me and he doesn't even need oil!

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.490
Help! Help!

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.500
Mom!

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:26.790
Machi.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.250
Where's the user manual and spec sheet?

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:33.710
I told you I wanted appliances with everything still in the boxes.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:35.630
I don't know. Yoshio was handling that.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.180
Ah...

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.060
We went overboard!

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.180
Geez...

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:49.270
What did you guys do? This is too much!

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:52.150
What? It wasn't my fault.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:56.360
It's Natsu's! He approached us without warning.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:00.780
Personally, I think the problem is Yoshio's setup.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:03.740
They need to know I won't eat them.

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:07.870
The Women's Association told me
that it's getting less scary every year.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:11.170
Acting normally, Natsu isn't scary enough.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.550
So it's your fault, Natsu.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.420
What? I'm doing my best!

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:19.300
The Gonzaburo before last was really, really scary.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:24.430
Numerous kids wet their pants and never behaved badly again.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:28.060
Oh, but Hiiko got put in the cell all the time.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:31.440
After a while, she wasn't scared at all.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:32.770
Hiiko?

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.900
Do you remember Hibiki from the Sakata family?

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.070
She came by today.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.070
What?

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:42.070
She took me clothes shopping.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.330
Oh, you guys already went to Shimomura?

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.370
Shimomura?

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.500
How do you know about that?

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:55.000
I'm the one who asked her to take you.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:58.720
Hii—

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:06.180
That's not true.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.610
I didn't do it for him!

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.070
Um...

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.120
Yeah, we know.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.700
You wouldn't do Yoshio any favors, right, Hibiki?

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:31.620
Yeah. I bet you'd die before doing Yoshio a favor.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.460
You were going to Shimomura anyway, right?

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:38.260
Right! And since you were going, you brought Machi along, right?

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:42.470
No... She didn't act like she had any business at Shimomura.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:48.220
And in the end, she did do what
Yoshio asked. She did him a favor.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:53.060
Hibiki, why did you do Yoshio a favor?

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.610
Machi!

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:25.390
The question is: Why did Hibiki do Yoshio a favor?

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:29.100
Why is that such a big deal?

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:34.060
Because Hibiki and I are different ages and have different personalities.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:37.690
We weren't close at all.
Today was our first real conversation.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:42.070
Who would take someone so different out shopping?

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:46.070
And we're talking about Hibiki. She even paid for gas.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:49.910
People wouldn't normally do that, even if asked.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:52.580
Not to mention it was Yoshio asking.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:56.960
I'd understand if she had business at Shimomura.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:02.260
But it didn't appear that way, and she wasn't familiar with Shimomura.

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:07.050
It's unnatural to do Yoshio a favor for no reason.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.760
I see...

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:15.060
You may be right. When I asked her to do it...

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:18.230
She said: "I'm not doing it."

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.820
So I was surprised to hear she did.

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:23.740
What'd you come to my work for?!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:28.370
By the way, I also wonder why Hiiko's always so cold to me.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:31.620
You must've done something to her.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.080
What do you mean by that?

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.580
You bother others to make them do what you want.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.500
You've always done that, Yoshio!

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:41.550
Hibiki, what're you gonna do?

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.550
You decide things without asking me!

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.010
Do about what?

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.050
When do I do that?

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.010
You know, well...

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:46.010
Constantly!

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:46.970
No, I don't!

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:49.970
You like Yoshio, right?

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:48.010
Yes, you do!

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.890
I don't!

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.510
I don't like him!

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:55.100
Don't say crazy stuff like that, you stupid bear!

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.690
The Gonzaburo told me about it.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:00.310
That damn geezer!

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.320
He said that in middle school,

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:07.240
the reason you teased Yoshio so much was because you liked him.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.240
That's wrong!

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:11.870
And in high school you would say things like, "He grown taller."

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.790
I did not!

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:17.250
You're wrong. That old bear was senile!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:20.500
I could never like someone as dimwitted as him!

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.170
Okay. I believe you.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.800
So why not take off your helmet?

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:31.010
You're not trying to hide your face because you're blushing, are you?

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:35.520
You have a calm face on under that helmet, right?

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.990
Of course I do, you damn bear!

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:55.410
She's pinching herself hard!
Her will to cover this up is amazing.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:15:01.420
Hey... I don't care what, but do something about this situation.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.290
I really didn't do anything!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.500
Well... I don't know.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:04.750
Liar!

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.170
I'm not lying.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:09.970
This is a good chance.
Why don't you tell him your feelings?

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:08.420
Think about it again!

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:15.260
Stop pushing it, you pervy bear!
How many times do I have to tell you?!

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.810
I'll kick your ass!

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:23.310
But Machi isn't taking the hint and Yoshio is...

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:24.360
Look.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.820
That expression signals that he's stopped thinking.

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:34.950
He'll never understand unless you say it straight.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.490
Really, look at him.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.290
I won't!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.330
Ah! This is your chance!

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:44.460
Yoshio's doing his own thing,

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:47.500
so you're free once you get past Machi.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.760
Seriously, what are you?

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.260
Hibiki...

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:58.310
Listen. You may feel uneasy talking to me about this,

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:04.900
but if Yoshio is causing you trouble, I'll help you.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.860
Let's do our best. We can beat him!

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:12.360
He must give her a rough time, too.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:15.660
You can't live like this, Hibiki!

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:21.660
He may have something on you,
but you should say what you want to say!

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:25.920
I know you can do it. Muster up your courage.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.550
Free your real self.

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:32.420
Hey, Natsu. What're you doing?

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:43.810
The Japanese heart, prizing harmony,
has evolved over centuries

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:47.610
and reached the level of a supernatural power

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:50.070
far beyond the understanding of foreigners.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.860
I want you to master this skill.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:55.950
This.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.750
There is only space between the lines.

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:07.040
I don't mean it literally. I'm talking about inferring others' feelings.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:12.260
It means understanding peoples' expressions and circumstances

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:15.800
to carry on a smooth conversation without ruining the mood.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.930
It's necessary in order to maintain good relationships with others.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:20.510
Why are you telling me this now?

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:26.520
You see, right now it's critical
that you read between the lines.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:31.280
Machi, since you're so convinced that Yoshio caused all this,

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:34.030
you're overlooking something important.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:37.660
I'm not in a position to spell it out for you,

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:41.870
so I want you to read between the lines to find the answer.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.160
Okay.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.540
Machi, I hate you!

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:55.170
Machi, I don't like you at all!

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.180
So don't get the wrong idea, okay?

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.850
Natsu is a bad actor.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:05.680
I always perform kagura with you,
but I could do it by myself!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.560
So my trial has already begun?

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:11.440
What should I do?

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:16.650
It's not like I want to do kagura with you, okay? It's not like that at all.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.830
That's not it.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.460
Machi!

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.170
I hate you, Machi!

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:40.970
Suppose I'm Hibiki and you're Yoshio.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.890
I hate you, okay?

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.480
Yoshio is gonna be strangled to death.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:58.990
Okay, Machi. There's someone Hibiki likes.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.450
I get it now.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.870
You do?

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.580
I had no idea.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:09.580
Right!

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:11.120
I was so oblivious.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:11.750
Right!

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:15.920
What have I done? I put Hibiki on the spot.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.130
I have to make amends right away.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:20.340
Right! Right!

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.550
So...

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:28.520
Reading between the lines here, what do you do?

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:40.400
I'm sorry, Hibiki, for not noticing. I was acting like a child.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:45.370
But now I know better. I'll free you!

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:51.160
Let Hibiki's lover go!

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:55.840
Wrong!

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.130
Argh!

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:05.260
Hibiki likes Yoshio!

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:08.930
Ah...

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:14.350
What? What about Hiiko and me?

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:24.950
H-Hibiki... Um...

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:32.460
Don't listen to him. It's just bearshit.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:36.710
If you tell anyone in the village, you'll pay for it.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.210
O-Okay.

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:40.630
Huh? What was that?

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:43.630
If you get me, speak up.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.800
I bwon berr abywon.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:48.890
I'm sorry, Machi. Bear it.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:54.390
A fear of delinquents has been hammered into Machi.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.650
Gosh... How could you not get it?

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:01.400
How could I?

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:05.780
Someone who <i>likes</i> Yoshio...

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:07.280
How terrible.

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.660
The world is a big place, isn't it, Natsu?

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.120
Yeah, it is.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:24.380
I wonder if I'll fall in love someday.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.760
I want to fall in love with a handsome man.

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:41.360
I'm breaking up with you...
so give the money back.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:47.320
Here! Are you happy now?
You really were a worthless woman!

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:49.370
This isn't all of it.

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:53.700
Natsu?

00:21:55.000 --> 00:22:00.170
Machi... Why don't you stay in this village forever?

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:01.460
No.

00:23:33.100 --> 00:23:34.440
Kumamiko-chan!

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:38.220
I'm hungry...

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:54.130
Kumamiko.
